pm_util version_3.0.10 2019_11_19
================================= 
- bugfix Jira ID PMCPESYS-166
   fix remaining banned c-function snprintf() -> sprintf_s().


pm_util version_3.0.9 2019_11_06
================================= 
- bugfix Jira ID PMCPESYS-162
   system command 'iwpriv', which was used to collect wifi power info,
   is not supported anymore from UGW. Instead 'iw <interface> iwlwav <cmd>
   must be used.
- Jira ID PMCPESYS-161
   all used safec-3 functions (*_s) must handle fail safe exit.
- Jira ID PMCPESYS-153
   minor change to avoid printing something to console in case system command
   failed. This is a useless info.


pm_util version_3.0.8 2019_10_02
================================= 
- add safec-3 support


pm_util version_3.0.7 2019_09_09
================================= 
- bugfix Jira ID PMCPESYS-151
   path problem with pwr_control.sh. pm_util must be called from
   the source directory of pwr_control.sh, which is /opt/intel/bin when using
   -e option which relates to pwr_control.sh.
- Jira ID PMCPESYS-129
   new feature: show entire clk tree (clk_summary)
- Jira ID PMCPESYS-140
   new feature: show wifi power related info + option to put on/off wifi PM
   AutoCoCMode
- Jira ID PMCPESYS-147
   new feature: start "pwr_control.sh" script to enable/disable all PM features
   and show current status of these devices
   add CPUFreq registered modules to -a option


pm_util version_3.0.6 2019_05_03
================================= 
- bug fix Jira ID PMCPESYS-138
   Redundant call of set governor and set frequency. Systems which have
   same clock source for all existing cpu's running Linux, the cpufreq framework
   provide just one /sys/devices/system/cpufreq/policy0 structure. No need to 
   specifiy cpu0, cpu1, cpu... because all of these are linked to same structure


